  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Minnesota received $73.3M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. The state recorded 1,769 awards with an average award size of $41.4K, and obligations fell 96.7% year over year. The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $30.6M and the Department of Agriculture obligated $23.6M, together accounting for the majority of FY2027 to date obligations. Cheese Manufacturing led industries with $14.6M in obligations, and ASSOCIATED MILK PRODUCERS INC received $8.8M, the largest vendor total. Historical obligations show a multi-year peak and decline: FY22 obligations were $2.5B, FY23 were $2.8B, FY24 were $3.3B, FY25 were $2.8B, and FY26 were $2.2B, compared with FY27 obligations of $73.3M. These figures are contract obligations and reflect a partial fiscal year to date total for FY2027. For contractors and procurement teams, the concentration of dollars in food production, construction, and medical services is notable for market targeting and capture planning.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What happened to Minnesota's federal contract spending in FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 96.7% year over year in FY2027 to date. Minnesota received $73.3M in obligations in FY2027 to date, down from $2.2B in FY26 and prior multi-year totals. The FY2027 to date total reflects a partial fiscal year and the count of reported awards is 1,769 with an average award size of $41.4K."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and industries dominate federal contracting in Minnesota right now?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $30.6M and the Department of Agriculture obligated $23.6M in FY2027 to date. Cheese Manufacturing is the largest industry with $14.6M and Commercial and Institutional Building Construction is second with $4.1M. ASSOCIATED MILK PRODUCERS INC is the top vendor with $8.8M."
      }
    ]
